---
import { getEntry, render } from 'astro:content';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/ui/SectionHead.astro';
import TechChip from '../components/ui/TechChip.astro';
import PlayGrid from '../components/play/PlayGrid.astro';
import { STACK_GROUPS } from '../data/technologies';
import { getPlayIndex } from '../lib/content';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { pages } from '../content/pages';

const about = await getEntry('about' as never, 'about' as never).catch(() => undefined);
const play = (await getPlayIndex()).slice(0, 4);
---
<SiteLayout title="About — Zack Low" description="Software engineer in Singapore, specialising in AI.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">{pages.about.eyebrow}</p>
      <h1 class="t-64">{pages.about.title}</h1>
      <p class="t-21 muted">{pages.about.lede}</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a href="/resume" class="btn btn-dark">Résumé</a>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-ghost">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="portrait">
      <img src="/img/portrait.jpg" alt="Zack Low" width="900" height="1125" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap prose">
    <p>I build full-stack systems, end to end: the database, the API, the screen,
      the deploy, and the bill at the end of the month. AI goes in
      <strong>where it earns its place</strong> — which, after a year of doing this
      professionally, is less often than the industry would like you to believe.</p>
    <p>The part I actually like is before any code gets written. Working out what is
      genuinely broken, who it is broken for, and what the smallest thing is that
      would fix it. Then owning that thing until it works in production — not until
      the ticket closes.</p>
    <p>The most useful thing I have built at work is
      <mark>a tracing dashboard</mark>, which is not a sentence anyone wants to hear.
      But you cannot make an agent cheaper or better until you can see what it is
      doing, and almost nobody builds that first. The most fun thing I have built is
      a camera app that deliberately makes you wait four minutes.</p>
    <p>Before Carro I spent a year at AI Singapore on generative 3D animation, did
      speech research at NIE, and wrote my first LLM tooling at the Department of
      Statistics back when nobody was calling it an agent. I studied Computer
      Science at NTU.</p>
    <p>Outside work I run a two-server homelab, climb badly, cook constantly, and
      shoot film. There is more of that on <a href="/play">Play</a>.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section band"><div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead title="Tech stack" sub="The stuff I use every week." />
    <div class="groups">
      {STACK_GROUPS.map((g) => (
        <div class="group">
          <h3 class="t-21">{g.title}</h3>
          <ul class="chips">{g.items.map((id) => <TechChip id={id} />)}</ul>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap">
    <SectionHead title="Play" sub="The other half." href="/play" linkLabel="All of it" />
    <PlayGrid items={play} />
  </div></section>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; align-items: stretch; background: var(--surface); }
  .copy {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s-4); justify-content: center;
    padding: clamp(48px, 8vw, 120px) var(--s-9) clamp(48px, 8vw, 120px) var(--gutter);
  }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: var(--s-3); flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: var(--s-2); }
  /* Full-bleed, no radius, no shadow — the pattern every good portrait hero uses. */
  .portrait { min-height: 560px; background: var(--border); }
  .portrait img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .groups { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .group {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: var(--s-7);
    align-items: start; padding-block: var(--s-6); border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-2); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .copy { padding-inline: var(--gutter); }
    .portrait { min-height: 360px; order: -1; }
    .group { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--s-3); }
  }
</style>
